++++++++++++++++++++++From 727f39e3e1f02709dc29ea4fabb41899dbd6981c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++++++++++++++++++++++From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
++++++++++++++++++++++Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 20:40:57 -0500
++++++++++++++++++++++Subject: [PATCH] tests : add test-rpc-server-multiclient
++++++++++++++++++++++
++++++++++++++++++++++Runs one rpc-server on loopback against several client processes, each
++++++++++++++++++++++with its own connection:
++++++++++++++++++++++
++++++++++++++++++++++- a second client's HELLO is answered while the first holds its
++++++++++++++++++++++  connection open, and probe-style connect/close doesn't disturb it
++++++++++++++++++++++- a SET_TENSOR outside its buffer closes only that connection
++++++++++++++++++++++- a client that FIN-closes before its reply is written doesn't SIGPIPE
++++++++++++++++++++++  the server
++++++++++++++++++++++- two clients computing at once get results matching the CPU backend,
++++++++++++++++++++++  with per-connection backends and with --serialize-compute
++++++++++++++++++++++- --max-clients rejects the extra connection and frees the slot after
++++++++++++++++++++++- running out of fds (ulimit -n 48, 100 connections) doesn't end the
++++++++++++++++++++++  accept loop
++++++++++++++++++++++- finished connections are reaped (active count back to 1)
++++++++++++++++++++++
++++++++++++++++++++++Each case fails against the server before the corresponding fix.
++++++++++++++++++++++Registered next to test-rpc-multi-server (label main, UNIX only).
++++++++++++++++++++++
++++++++++++++++++++++Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
