++++++++++++++++++++From 4727d61e04118f8512e94432778ca4dd0faf97a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++++++++++++++++++++From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
++++++++++++++++++++Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 01:12:20 -0500
++++++++++++++++++++Subject: [PATCH] common : split-balance: time the dominant weight type, model
++++++++++++++++++++ n_batch drains
++++++++++++++++++++
++++++++++++++++++++The calibration timed the type of layer 0's ffn_up. In mixed-quant files
++++++++++++++++++++that is often not representative: Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q4_K_XL has q3_K there,
++++++++++++++++++++which made the 780M look 6x slower than the 8060S for decode instead of
++++++++++++++++++++the ~2.6x measured on the real layers (now q5_K, 3.4x).
++++++++++++++++++++
++++++++++++++++++++The prefill model assumed one pipeline over the whole prompt, but every
++++++++++++++++++++llama_decode() call (n_batch tokens) drains it. Model the drain per
++++++++++++++++++++call; the workload gets n_batch from the context params.
++++++++++++++++++++
++++++++++++++++++++Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
