++++++++++Subject: [PATCH] chat : K2-Horizon: accept any effort's close tag as the end
++++++++++ of reasoning
++++++++++
++++++++++K2-Horizon's template opens the reasoning with the tag for the request's
++++++++++reasoning_effort (the fleet pins "low": <ifm|think_faster>), and the parser
++++++++++workaround registered only the matching close tag. The model often closes a
++++++++++"low" reasoning block with the "high" tag </ifm|think> instead, so the parser
++++++++++never found the end: the whole reply went to reasoning_content, with the raw
++++++++++tag in it, and content came back empty (live on gabesrv06/10, 2026-09-25, in
++++++++++5/5 requests through LiteLLM and direct).
++++++++++
++++++++++analyze_reasoning gains end_alts, extra tags that also close the reasoning;
++++++++++the K2-Horizon workaround lists the other two effort tags there. The test
++++++++++covers all three close tags at "low" and fails without the change.
++++++++++
++++++++++Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
