++++++From 649e5e50a3d944c4469dc963a150d07fbe58b856 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++++++From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
++++++Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:22:02 -0500
++++++Subject: [PATCH] server : a captured checkpoint may outlive its task: don't
++++++ read slot.task for it
++++++
++++++Fleet QA round 7 (Dawn): a multi-device master segfaulted on the second of
++++++two back-to-back requests (NULL read in create_checkpoint,
++++++server-context.cpp:2419, `slot.task->id`). A request that ends right after
++++++its prompt decode (n_predict 1, EOS or a stop as the first token) releases
++++++its slot while that slot's in-batch capture is still pending, since captures
++++++are read only after a later decode. The next task's create_captured_checkpoints
++++++then made the checkpoint with the slot's task already reset.
++++++
++++++The capture now records the id of the task that submitted it, and
++++++create_checkpoint uses that instead of slot.task (still slot.task for
++++++checkpoints made directly). Reproduced and verified under ASan with
++++++LLAMA_SERVER_CKPT_CAPTURE=1 on Qwen3.5-4B: 4/4 back-to-back n_predict 1
++++++requests, where the second one used to crash.
++++++
++++++Only multi-device masters capture by default, so the single-device
++++++production masters were not exposed.
++++++
++++++Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
