++++From 1b177d4e5fbbc5b3d5805be75c7f262e59b73140 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++++From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
++++Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:45:26 -0500
++++Subject: [PATCH] chat : K2-Horizon: don't leak tool-call markup into content
++++ with no tools
++++
++++Round 7 QA found K2-Horizon sometimes emits tool-call markup
++++(</ifm|arg_value>, </ifm|tool_call>, </ifm|tool_calls>) even when the
++++request has no tools. analyze_content::build_parser only runs once tools
++++are ruled out for parsing, and the existing K2 workaround's stray_ends
++++only listed the reasoning close-tag variants, so this markup landed in
++++content verbatim (5 replies in the round-7 batch).
++++
++++Add stray_ends_no_tools alongside stray_ends: same "end content there,
++++drop the rest" and stop_after_reasoning handling, but only folded in
++++when the request has no tools, so real tool calls (tools offered) are
++++never affected -- analyze_tools still parses the same tags as syntax.
++++
++++Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5
++++---
++++ common/chat-auto-parser-generator.cpp | 19 ++++++++++--
++++ common/chat-auto-parser.h             |  5 ++++
++++ common/chat-diff-analyzer.cpp         |  8 +++++
