++++From b4a0f6c8514b59daea16c37e1ea27fb4a80c58ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
++++From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
++++Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:56:24 -0500
++++Subject: [PATCH] common : split-balance: fix calibration overrating a device
++++ under per-node Vulkan submits
++++
++++The untimed-op probe (t_op_tg/t_op_pp, a chain of scale ops pricing a
++++layer's norms/RoPE/elementwise nodes per node) was only 64 nodes long.
++++On a backend that submits one command buffer per node
++++(GGML_VK_MAX_NODES_PER_SUBMIT=1, the DeviceLost mitigation this fork
++++already carries for gfx90c), that chain is too short to reach the
++++submit-queue depth a real decode/prefill graph runs at, so it measured
++++the cheap, unsaturated per-submit cost instead of the real one and
++++calibration overrated the device -- 6-8x on gfx90c for dense q4_K
++++models (K2-Horizon-7B, Qwen3.5-4B), which then put every layer on it
++++under --split-balance auto.
++++
++++Fix: lengthen the chain to 256 nodes (8x amdgpu's 32-job sched_jobs
++++ring). This needed calibrate_device's ggml_context sizing to account
++++for the chain's own tensors too -- the untouched budget was tight
++++enough that a MoE model with an output layer configured (gpt-oss-20b)
++++overflowed it and crashed. Added a regression test for that
++++(test_calibrate_context_memory_budget, a synthetic one-layer MoE model
++++on the CPU backend, no GPU needed).
++++
++++Verified on an RTX 3080 Ti Laptop GPU: the real per-node submit cost is
++++much smaller there than on gfx90c's weak amdgpu ring, so the
++++predicted/measured gap the env var causes is only ~10-19%, not 6-8x,
++++but it now moves in the right direction and by roughly the right
++++amount for K2-Horizon-7B, Qwen3.5-4B and gpt-oss-20b, with no
++++regression when the env var is unset. See FLEET.md for the full
++++writeup, including what still needs gfx90c hardware to confirm.
++++
++++Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5
